/target
/book/book

# Fetched by `vale sync`; not vendored. Run `vale sync` after cloning.
/.vale/styles/Google

# Written by `insta` when an inline snapshot fails locally, and consumed
# by `cargo insta review`; it's scratch state for that one run, not
# something to commit. CI never produces one — INSTA_UPDATE=no in
# .github/workflows/ci.yml stops insta writing pending snapshots there.
*.pending-snap

# Written by `TRYCMD=dump cargo test -p hl-cli --test cli_tests`, which
# dumps every transcript's real output for inspection instead of
# comparing it. Scratch state for one run, same as insta's pending
# snapshots; CI never produces one, since TRYCMD is pinned to a
# non-writing value in .github/workflows/ci.yml.
/crates/hl-cli/dump/
